pr_reviews_excerpt:
@dwnusbaum (COMMENTED): @orgi Sorry I did not have a chance to review the PR yet in detail. I am not very familiar with the load balancer API, but the PR seems fine to me overall, although there are a few things that would be good to clean up.
---
@dwnusbaum (APPROVED): Sorry for not getting back sooner on this. Updating the baseline seems fine to me at this point, but I want to release the plugin one last time before updating the baseline. Part of my hesitancy over merging this sooner was that I thought there might be scenarios where after this change, Pipelines would wait to build on a node with affinity instead of using another available node, but the test case I had in mind had the same behavior with and without this change, so I am not worried about that scenario anymore. Test case in question:
```java
@Issue("JENKINS-36547")
@Test public void shouldNotWaitToUseSameAgentIfOtherAgentsFree() {
    story.then(r -> {
        for (int i = 0; i < 2; i++) {
            DumbSlave slave = r.createOnlineSlave();
            slave.setLabelString("foo");
        }

        WorkflowJob p1 = r.jenkins.createProject(WorkflowJob.class, "demo1");
        p1.setDefinition(new CpsFlowDefinition("node('foo') {}", true));

        WorkflowRun run1 = r.assertBuildStatusSuccess(p1.scheduleBuild2(0));
        String node1 = getWorkspaceActions(run1).get(0).getNode();

        WorkflowJob p2 = r.jenkins.createProject(WorkflowJob.class, "demo2");
        p2.setDefinition(new CpsFlowDefinition("node('"+node1+"') { semaphore 'sem' }", true));
        WorkflowRun run2 = p2.scheduleBuild2(0).waitForStart();
        SemaphoreStep.waitForStart("sem/1", run2);

        // I thought that before this change, this line would complete since the build would take place on the free node, but in fact it waits for `slave0` (which is occupied by the sleeping build), and so the test time out. Since the behavior is unchanged this shouldn't be a problem.
        WorkflowRun run3 = r.assertBuildStatusSuccess(p1.scheduleBuild2(0));
        String node2 = getWorkspaceActions(run3).get(0).getNode();

        assertThat(node1, not(equalTo(node2)));
    });
}
```

